nts":7,"created_at":"2025-03-14T14:33:57Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T16:59:41Z","closed_at":"2025-09-16T16:57:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducable in 4.3-4.4-Stable, not able to test earlier versions at the moment.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Arch Linux #1 ZEN SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sat, 08 Feb 2025 18:54:38 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) UHD Graphics 620 (KBL GT2) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-8650U CPU @ 1.90GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using Volumetric Fog with a Spotlight Node, the Volumetric Fog typically meets the Spotlight Node without Shadows enabled. With shadows on, the fog doesn't meet the node like it does without shadows, as demonstrated by the screenshots below (Green is without Shadows, Red is with Shadows).\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/378efd9f-cf7f-4691-94fa-8b736c3bfba6)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0fbd8ba3-bca7-4443-ae12-ad34b58d9b7a)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set `volumetric_fog_enabled` to True in WorldEnvironment\n2. Set `volumetric_fog_temporal_reprojection_enabled` to False in WorldEnvironment\n3. Set `rendering/environment/volumetric_fog/use_filter` to False in Project Settings\n4.  Add a Spotlight Node with a high `light_volumetric_fog_energy` Value (1000)\n5. Enable Shadows\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[volumetrics.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19249169/volumetrics.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/